---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { APP } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';

const trail = [{ label: 'About', href: '/about/' }];
---

<Base
  title="About Plantive: Plant Identification and Care"
  description="Who makes Plantive, how our plant care guides are researched and reviewed, and the editorial standards we hold them to."
  canonical="/about/"
  schema={[breadcrumbs(trail)]}
>
  <div class="wrap hub-head">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />
    <h1>About Plantive</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Plantive is a plant identification and plant care app for iPhone, made by {APP.developer}. This
      site is its free companion library of care guides.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap wrap-prose prose about">
    <h2>What we are trying to do</h2>
    <p>
      Watering and light are two common sources of houseplant problems. Both are easier to assess
      when you know what the plant is and can compare its conditions with species-specific guidance.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is the gap Plantive is built for. Identification on its own is a novelty. Identification
      that leads straight to <em>this species wants its top two inches dry, and it needs to be within
      six feet of that window</em> is genuinely useful.
    </p>

    <h2>How these guides are made</h2>
    <p>
      Plantive maintains the guides and is adding visible horticultural and botanical references to
      the pages where they are most useful. We aim for practical checks rather than false certainty:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Conditions before calendars.</strong> Check the potting mix, light, season and plant
        response before treating a watering interval as a rule.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Honest difficulty.</strong> We call fiddle leaf figs and calatheas demanding, because
        they are, rather than describing everything as easy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Symptom-first troubleshooting.</strong> Use observable signs to narrow the causes,
        and keep the diagnosis tentative when several causes look alike.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Transparent update dates.</strong> You can see when a guide was published and when its
        content was last changed.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where advice is genuinely contested, we say so. Where a popular claim does not hold up (that
      snake plants meaningfully purify the air in a real room, or that misting fixes humidity), we
      say that too.
    </p>

    <h2>Toxicity and safety</h2>
    <p>
      We include toxicity information on every plant guide because it matters in homes with pets and
      children. It is general guidance, not veterinary advice.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>If an animal or child has eaten part of a plant, contact a vet or poison control line
      immediately.</strong> Do not spend time identifying the plant first. Bring it with you or send
      a photo, and let them identify it while treatment begins.
    </p>

    <h2>The app</h2>
    <p>
      {APP.name} is free to download and requires iOS {APP.minimumOsVersion} or later. Optional Pro
      subscriptions and lifetime purchases are available in the app; current terms and prices are
      shown on the App Store listing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Subscriptions and refunds are handled by Apple. To cancel, open Settings on your iPhone, tap
      your name, then Subscriptions. For refunds, visit reportaproblem.apple.com.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections, questions and feedback are all welcome at
      <EmailLink />. If you spot something wrong in a
      care guide, please tell us. We would rather fix it than have it sit there.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plantive is published by {APP.developer}. Read our
      <a href={APP.privacyUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a> and
      <a href={APP.termsUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">terms of use</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <CtaBand source="page-cta" />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hub-head {
    padding-top: 2.25rem;
  }

  .hub-head h1 {
    margin-block: 1rem 0.9rem;
  }

  .about {
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
